# .harness/target.conf — the target's declared world (copy to target.conf per target).
# proof.sh refuses to run without the real file: a factory that cannot bring the
# system up cannot prove "done", and that gap is declared, never silently passed.
#
# provision: brings the environment up. Runs with PROOF_DIR exported — write any
#   setup evidence there. For a web app this might be `docker compose up -d --wait`
#   or a script that mints a disposable preview environment. NEVER production.
# probe: named entry points exercised for real, one per line, `name:: command`.
#   Each is receipted; nonzero exit = proof failure. Screenshots, videos, DB
#   checks out of band, curl hits — anything that captures proof-of-doing.
# access: where a human finds entry points, URLs, and credentials docs to click
#   and test after the run.
# teardown: always runs, even after failure.
#
# Example (web service):
# provision: docker compose -f compose.preview.yml up -d --wait
# probe: health:: curl -fsS http://localhost:8080/healthz
# probe: create-item:: curl -fsS -X POST http://localhost:8080/items -d '{"name":"x"}' -H 'content-type: application/json'
# probe: item-in-db:: psql "$PREVIEW_DSN" -tAc "select count(*) from items where name='x'" | grep -qx 1
# probe: screenshot:: npx playwright screenshot http://localhost:8080 "$PROOF_DIR/home.png"
# access: docs/preview-access.md
# teardown: docker compose -f compose.preview.yml down -v
#
# Example (this repo — a library: its "environment" is the gate suite in a fresh
# checkout, which endgame.sh already runs; a target.conf is still worth declaring
# once there is a consuming service to stand up):
# provision: true
# probe: import:: .venv/bin/python -c 'import factory_core, factory_runtime'
# probe: cli:: .venv/bin/python -m factory_runtime.cli status --help
# access: README.md
# teardown: true
